kind=LITERAL	edgeRole=ROOT	rootContext=MODULE_LEVEL_STATEMENT	expressionOwnerKind=METHOD	pyTypeLinkHash=	expressionOwnerHash=PY_METHOD_57b34b04c8f99b558638ddf8a40a1baa	parentExpressionHash=	position=0	depth=0	literalType=STRING	literalValue="Private name mangling (`__name` -> `_ClassName__name`), pinned down at the boundary CPython actually draws it at, rather than the commonly mis-stated ""any double-underscore attribute"" version: - It mangles the identifier **textually**, recursively through every nested def/lambda/comprehension inside the class body, using the *nearest enclosing class* at that point in the source — not the outermost one. - It applies to bare identifiers (which show up as mangled symtable symbols — Gate-1 checkable) exactly the same way it applies to attribute-access names like `self.__x` (`ast.Attribute.attr` is left UNMANGLED by `ast.parse`; the substitution only happens later, in bytecode compilation's `co_names`). That second form is confirmed against `compile()`/`dis` below but is invisible to both `ast` and `symtable`, so it is not something Gate 1 or Gate 2 can adjudicate — flagged in the manifest, not asserted as oracle-verified. - Exactly two leading underscores and *at most one* trailing underscore qualifies. Two leading AND two-or-more trailing (a ""dunder"", e.g. `__init__`, `__x__`) is explicitly exempt."	comprehensionKind=NONE	unaryFixity=NONE	operatorString=	referencedEntityKind=UNKNOWN	referencedEntityHash=	lambdaScopeHash=	potentialQualifiedName=	isAmbiguous=false	returnStatementIndex=	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=20	endColumn=3	pyScopeLinkHash=PY_SCOPE_821aeba8a746c6ac062dcb1a4e10b28b	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_75dd800d24b53dd3ca1d826ca1525876	bindingLinkHash=	nameContext=LOAD	isWrite=false	argumentKeywordName=	isAwaited=false	isStarred=false	dottedPath=	inferredTypeName=str	inferredTypeKind=BUILTIN_SCALAR	inferenceEvidence=LITERAL	inferenceConfidence=CERTAIN	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyExpressionUniqueHash=PY_EXPRESSION_2cec14bdd1c83115c6307c08b221e265
kind=LITERAL	edgeRole=ROOT	rootContext=MODULE_LEVEL_STATEMENT	expressionOwnerKind=METHOD	pyTypeLinkHash=	expressionOwnerHash=PY_METHOD_6fa4ea82d6c14c10951458a04c0851cd	parentExpressionHash=	position=0	depth=0	literalType=STRING	literalValue=Closes the remaining Gate-3 node-type gap that isn't `match`: assert, break/continue, elif chains, implicit string concatenation, f-string interpolation forms (literal `{{`/`}}` escapes, a nested dynamic format spec, and a plain format spec), backslash line continuation, `not`, a plain set display, slice forms, and a typed parameter with a default value. Each construct was confirmed against `ast.parse` before staging; none of this is exotic, it is simply syntax the mined corpus's six projects happened not to phrase this way often enough to be sampled.	comprehensionKind=NONE	unaryFixity=NONE	operatorString=	referencedEntityKind=UNKNOWN	referencedEntityHash=	lambdaScopeHash=	potentialQualifiedName=	isAmbiguous=false	returnStatementIndex=	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=9	endColumn=3	pyScopeLinkHash=PY_SCOPE_72da2fafab9ca96d9c1e8f5754d35ea5	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_99797da9f6b8580a03c8a2f7bf6898ea	bindingLinkHash=	nameContext=LOAD	isWrite=false	argumentKeywordName=	isAwaited=false	isStarred=false	dottedPath=	inferredTypeName=str	inferredTypeKind=BUILTIN_SCALAR	inferenceEvidence=LITERAL	inferenceConfidence=CERTAIN	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyExpressionUniqueHash=PY_EXPRESSION_89ff258e89fd481a0d8b5d039d26f3de
